---
// UNLISTED, LINK-ONLY PAGE. Not linked from the public site, excluded from the
// sitemap (astro.config.mjs filter), noindex/nofollow meta + X-Robots-Tag
// header (netlify.toml "/p/*"). Do not add to nav, llms.txt, or any links.
// Anyone with the link can read this public listing brief. No login.
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import heritageLogo from "../../../assets/heritage-logo.png";

const pageTitle = "Spring City - Wind Walker Ranch Properties";

const sources = [
  {
    label: "UtahRealEstate.com MLS #2184902",
    href: "https://www.utahrealestate.com/2184902/direction/11550++PIGEON+HOLLOW+RD/location/Spring+City+UT+84662",
  },
  {
    label: "Compass listing",
    href: "https://www.compass.com/homedetails/11550-Pigeon-Hollow-Rd-Spring-City-UT-84662/2851O9_pid/",
  },
  {
    label: "SLC Homes listing",
    href: "https://search.slchomes.com/details-res?listingid=2184902",
  },
];

const facts: [string, string][] = [
  ["MLS list price", "$3,975,000 for the advertised ~100-acre offering only"],
  ["MLS", "#2184902"],
  ["Address", "11550 Pigeon Hollow Rd, Spring City, UT 84662"],
  ["Holding reported by Mike", "169.06 acres under common ownership. Not the priced MLS offer."],
];

const checks = [
  "Sale scope and terms. Whether the full holding will be sold, which boundaries are included, and the price for that holding. The $3,975,000 figure is the MLS price for the advertised acreage only.",
  "Water inventory. Rights, shares, wells, what is included, transfer, and how water would be allocated if portions are sold later.",
  "Buffer-zone development parameters. The Spring City buffer map, jurisdiction, zoning, permitted density, subdivision requirements, access, and water and septic approvals.",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  exactTitle={true}
  description="Unlisted property brief for Spring City - Wind Walker Ranch Properties. MLS #2184902 lists about 100 acres at $3,975,000. Acquisition concept is the larger common-owner holding reported by Mike. Confirm scope, price, and water."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="bg-navy px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <p class="font-heading text-xs sm:text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold mb-3">Unlisted property brief</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-white leading-tight">{pageTitle}</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg sm:text-xl text-cream/95">11550 Pigeon Hollow Rd, Spring City, UT 84662</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base sm:text-lg text-cream/80">
        Wind Walker Homestead · MLS #2184902 · Listed at $3,975,000
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base sm:text-lg text-cream leading-relaxed">
        Whole-property acquisition. Buy the common-owner holding, keep the land and water you want, and sell off what you do not.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="h-1 bg-gold"></div>

  <section class="px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-14">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10">
      <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-10 order-2 lg:order-1">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Whole-property acquisition</h2>
          <p class="text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            The concept is to acquire the entire common-owner holding, retain the desired land and water, and sell non-core portions and improvements to recover capital.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            Mike’s review of Sanpete County records identified 169.06 acres under common ownership. The MLS currently advertises approximately 100 acres, subject to a boundary adjustment, at $3,975,000. That price applies to the advertised MLS offering only.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            Willingness to sell the full holding, the price for it, and the water included with it have to be confirmed. This is a proposed acquisition strategy. It is not the listing’s current sale terms, and it is not an approved subdivision.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Land, water, and what you keep</h2>
          <p class="text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            The hold is control of the acreage you retain, with the water that serves it. Buildings and surplus land are candidates to sell after closing, not the reason to buy.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            Mike reports additional water is available with the sale; exact rights, quantities, included interests and transfer terms remain to be documented.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            The listing also mentions 3.00 water shares and two wells. That note is not the water inventory. The amount of additional water is unknown. Nothing here promises supply, yield, or that every right conveys.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            Selling buildings or non-core acreage depends on legal boundaries, approvals, access, and water allocation. No resale yield, return, or timeline is stated.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Development position</h2>
          <p class="text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            Mike reports that part of the property lies within the Spring City buffer zone and allows development. Confirm the applicable jurisdiction, zoning, permitted density, subdivision requirements, access and water/septic approvals before underwriting a development plan.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            That report is not an entitled subdivision and not a lot yield.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Confirm these three</h2>
          <ol class="space-y-3 list-decimal pl-5 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            {checks.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>

        <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          {facts.map(([label, value]) => (
            <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-4 shadow-sm border border-navy/5">
              <dt class="font-heading text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-gold font-semibold">{label}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-navy leading-relaxed">{value}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-navy mb-3 pb-2 border-b-2 border-gold/60">Buildings, as context</h2>
          <p class="text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            The listing describes lodging, event space, and ranch buildings, including a main house, plus retreat and short-term rental use. Useful if a later sale of improvements is part of the plan. Not the acquisition thesis.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            The listing states lodging and event income of $170,000–$186,000 a year. That is listing-reported income, not verified net income.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-navy mb-3 pb-2 border-b-2 border-gold/60">Public sources</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {sources.map((source) => (
              <li>
                <a href={source.href} class="text-navy underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-gold break-words" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.label}</a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-navy/70 leading-relaxed">
            Unlisted brief for anyone with this link. Mike Price, REALTOR&reg;, Heritage Realty Group, is the local contact. Mike’s acreage, water, and buffer notes are his reports, not a survey, a water decree, or an approval. This is not an appraisal or a zoning opinion.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="lg:col-span-1 order-1 lg:order-2">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 bg-navy text-white rounded-lg p-6 shadow-md">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
            <img src="/images/site/mike-headshot.jpg" alt="Mike Price, REALTOR®" width="80" height="80" class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-gold" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <div>
              <p class="font-display text-xl">Mike Price</p>
              <p class="text-cream/80 text-sm">REALTOR&reg;</p>
              <p class="text-cream/80 text-sm">Heritage Realty Group, LLC</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-cream/90 mb-4">Questions about this listing? Contact Mike.</p>
          <address class="not-italic text-cream/80 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            P.O. Box 431<br />
            Spring City, UT 84662
          </address>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <a href="tel:4356600401" class="block text-center bg-gold text-navy font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm px-4 py-3 rounded hover:bg-white transition-colors">Call or Text 435-660-0401</a>
            <a href="mailto:mikesellsut@gmail.com?subject=Spring%20City%20-%20Wind%20Walker%20Ranch%20Properties%20(MLS%20%232184902)" class="block text-center border border-gold text-gold font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm px-4 py-3 rounded hover:bg-gold hover:text-navy transition-colors break-words">Email mikesellsut@gmail.com</a>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-white/15 flex justify-center">
            <div class="bg-white rounded px-3 py-2">
              <Image src={heritageLogo} alt="Heritage Realty Group, LLC" width={200} class="h-12 w-auto" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto text-xs text-navy/60 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <p>Listing courtesy of Berkshire Hathaway HomeServices Utah Properties (St George) / Lance May. Source: public MLS #2184902.</p>
      <p>Information is not guaranteed. The $3,975,000 price is the MLS price for the advertised acreage. Full-holding availability, price, boundaries, and included water are unconfirmed. Disposition of buildings or surplus acreage depends on boundaries, approvals, access, and water allocation.</p>
      <p>Mike Price, REALTOR&reg; | Heritage Realty Group, LLC | P.O. Box 431, Spring City, UT 84662 | Agent License 5957476-LA00 | Brokerage License 6232680-CN00</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
